    "conclusion": "Content-feature root cause (Protocol_TCP, Tcp_flags_reset_Set, frame_len) formally confirmed via Captum Integrated Gradients, consistent with Part J. Topology importance is also supported as low by both GNNExplainer and PGExplainer. GNNExplainer produced a low and stable edge-mask maximum (0.2922, std=0.0023), while PGExplainer produced a lower edge-mask maximum (0.1250, std=0.0426). The low GNNExplainer node-mask saturation fraction (0.0113, 1.13%) confirms that the sparse explanation converged successfully rather than failing to optimize. Therefore, the analyzed false positives are primarily associated with packet-content features rather than graph topology. Topology-explainer scores and Integrated Gradients attributions measure different quantities and are therefore interpreted as complementary evidence rather than directly compared numerically."
  },
  "week10_temporal_streaming": {
    "motivation": "Weeks 2-9 evaluate SCADANet using a graph constructed from the full dataset before training. Week 10 introduces a discrete-time temporal evaluation by ordering flows chronologically, dividing them into equal-flow-count windows, tracking cumulative IP-pair edge arrival, and using an early-vs-late train/test split. The result is contrasted against the Week 6-9 IP-held-out protocol.",
